<p>Benin&#x27;s finance minister, Romuald Wadagni, won the country&#x27;s presidential election with about 94% of the vote, according to provisional results announced after the April 12 ballot. Even before the full count was complete, opposition candidate Paul Hounkpe conceded defeat. The lopsided result left little immediate sign of a post-election challenge as provisional counting continued.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/DgzVi-3Y45aAw-zAXsoz900s1RzpCPpFCYoqcDyqqFA4ws5gOH-3njF1TMDIQkW7QjH75AlrGLX6Grx7ljXxYf1R5EOIGoS22JRc2OxQSGLShOEyZsvky5MaGF0-9pIc_uFvfKqR5OJRcEvkyKM0ZoShPj4ILbO9SpCgztGGJ-hQ09o2pP9brkMS4iva-CyLwqxs1c1bNXpoJDOHZqT5uZfwuf9nHkXpfKatiuHNvqkJ518P3z1KRu42Iw' alt='Presidential candidate Romuald Wadagni greets supporters at a campaign rally in Cotonou, Benin, Friday, on April 10, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Election favorite: Reports described Wadagni as the favorite before all votes were tallied, showing how expected his win was even before the scale of it became clear.</li><li>Opposition field: Paul Hounkpe was the race&#x27;s sole opposition candidate, reflecting how narrow the electoral field had become by voting day.</li><li>Security challenge: Coverage highlighted northern Benin as a serious security concern for the incoming administration.</li><li>Economic test: Reports said Wadagni will also face pressure over living standards, making household economic conditions an early measure of his presidency.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Paul Hounkpe: He conceded defeat to Wadagni after the vote, signaling that he accepted the provisional outcome rather than mounting an immediate challenge. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/opposition-candidate-concedes-defeat-to-wadagni-in-benin-presidential-race'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Electoral commission: It published provisional results that put Wadagni in a landslide lead, providing the official basis for reports of his victory. (<a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/benins-finance-minister-wadagni-wins-presidential-election-with-94-landslide-2026-04-13/'>Reuters</a>)</li><li>International media analysis: Al Jazeera described Wadagni as the government candidate and said the scale of the result gave him a strong starting mandate. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/13/government-candidate-wadagni-on-course-to-win-benin-presidential-vote'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202604140093.html'>Benin: Benin&#x27;s Finance Minister Wins Presidential Election with 94%</a> - allafrica.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/benin-s-finance-minister-wins-presidential-election-with-94/a-76769500'>Benin&#x27;s finance minister wins presidential election with 94%</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/14/benin-elects-presidential-favorite-romuald-wadagni_6752390_4.html'>Benin elects presidential favorite Romuald Wadagni</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/13/government-candidate-wadagni-on-course-to-win-benin-presidential-vote'>Benin’s Wadagni wins presidential election with landslide 94% of votes</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/benins-wadagni-wins-presidency-in-landslide-with-over-94-of-votes'>Benin&#x27;s Wadagni wins presidency in landslide with over 94% of votes</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/benins-finance-minister-wadagni-wins-presidential-election-with-94-landslide-2026-04-13/'>Provisional results reveal that finance minister Romuald Wadagni won in a landslide victory with 94% of the vote.</a> - reuters.com</li></ul>